[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/513188-CSLib/topic/PMF.20monad.20and.20discrete.20probability/near/585928283\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If we write the program in FreeM, then can we lift it to a <code>Measure</code> via <code>Measure.bind</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm not sure if the answer is actually \"yes\"; does this work?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbQuery</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sample</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbQuery</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I worry that this somehow still leaves us missing one of the two MeasureSpaces needed by <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasureTheory.Measure.bind#doc\">docs#MeasureTheory.Measure.bind</a></p>",
        "id": 585930359,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776352412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>See : <a href=\"https://github.com/Shreyas4991/Algolean/blob/main/Algolean/Models/RandomSample.lean\">https://github.com/Shreyas4991/Algolean/blob/main/Algolean/Models/RandomSample.lean</a></p>",
        "id": 585930567,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776352460
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The distribution gnostic variant of this would be yours.</p>",
        "id": 585930683,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776352488
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm specifically asking if this still works for <code>Measure</code> as opposed to <code>PMF</code></p>",
        "id": 585930688,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776352490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I fear it might run into trouble for the same reason that there can't be a <code>Monad</code> instance on <code>Measure</code></p>",
        "id": 585930787,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776352512
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It should if your Progs have the MeasrableSpace instance</p>",
        "id": 585930793,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776352513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You want a parameter type in the query though</p>",
        "id": 585931128,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776352595
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Something like :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbQuery</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sample</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">dist</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Measure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbQuery</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 585931243,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1776352620
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interpreting that optimistically, maybe you can get the measure space for every type but the result from the query, and you pass the final measure space into the function from FreeM to Measure</p>",
        "id": 585931455,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1776352664
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you try it as a PR to Algolean, maybe with examples in the test folder?</p>",
        "id": 585931885,
